====================================================================================================
IS THE PLATEAU REAL, OR DID v14 FREEZE R?
====================================================================================================
  Matched TOTAL shots T. QLTO spends T over G*L circuits, parameter-shift
  over 2MG. QLTO is given the ORACLE best R on the grid at each budget.
  v14 held R=0.6 at every budget and reported a plateau at cos ~ 0.977.

  Heisenberg N=4:  M=24  G=3  L=6   QLTO 18 circuits,  p-shift 144 circuits  (8x)
     T total     S_q    S_p     R*   cos QLTO    cos PS   1-cos QL   1-cos PS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
        8192     455     56   0.60     0.8784    0.8778    0.12163    0.12219
       32768    1820    227   0.45     0.9572    0.9638    0.04276    0.03621
      131072    7281    910   0.45     0.9825    0.9904    0.01747    0.00962
      524288   29127   3640   0.45     0.9947    0.9975    0.00531    0.00246
  fitted (1-cos) ~ T^alpha:   QLTO alpha = -0.742    p-shift alpha = -0.941
  R* trend: 0.60 -> 0.45 -> 0.45 -> 0.45

  Heisenberg N=6:  M=36  G=3  L=6   QLTO 18 circuits,  p-shift 216 circuits  (12x)
     T total     S_q    S_p     R*   cos QLTO    cos PS   1-cos QL   1-cos PS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
        8192     455     37   0.60     0.8282    0.7348    0.17184    0.26524
       32768    1820    151   0.60     0.9410    0.9139    0.05905    0.08607
      131072    7281    606   0.45     0.9763    0.9769    0.02365    0.02307
      524288   29127   2427   0.45     0.9930    0.9942    0.00700    0.00584
  fitted (1-cos) ~ T^alpha:   QLTO alpha = -0.759    p-shift alpha = -0.921
  R* trend: 0.60 -> 0.60 -> 0.45 -> 0.45

  READING IT. alpha ~ 0 for QLTO means the plateau is REAL and the
  withdrawal in the notes stands. alpha clearly negative, with R* SHRINKING
  as T grows, means v14's plateau was an artefact of freezing R and the
  shot question has to be reopened.

  THE EXPONENTS TO EXPECT, and note the metric SQUARES them. The algebra
  gives R* ~ T^(-1/6) and gradient ERROR ~ T^(-1/3) for QLTO against the
  unbiased T^(-1/2). But 1-cos ~ (1/2)(e_perp/|g|)^2 for small errors, so
  it tracks error SQUARED and the fitted alpha should be:
        QLTO      alpha ~ -2/3 = -0.667
        p-shift   alpha ~ -1.0
  A QLTO alpha near -2/3 confirms the bias-variance trade is live and the
  plateau was the protocol. A QLTO alpha near 0 confirms the floor is real.
